---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmailSignup from '../components/EmailSignup.astro';
---

<Base
  title="For authors"
  description="You wrote the book. Murmmers Press carries it the rest of the way: the edit that keeps your voice, the cover, the files, the ISBNs, every shop, the launch. A full-service house run by AI agents, with your hand on every gate."
>
  <section class="how-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">For authors</p>
      <h1>You wrote the book. That was meant to be the hard part.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Then came the cover that would not pass. The spine three millimetres too narrow. The ISBN a checkbox quietly handed to Amazon, so no other shop would take it. The launch day that arrived, and passed, in silence. You are a writer. Somewhere along the way someone handed you a second job you never trained for, and never wanted.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-pull">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="big">The writing was the part you were built for. No one warned you about the rest.</p>
      <p>Getting a finished book onto the shelves is not one task. It is fifty small, unforgiving, technical ones, and every single one of them can bounce your book back to the start. None of them are writing. All of them stand between your book and a reader.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The wall every author meets</h2>
      <p class="pl-intro">We know these by name, because we have stood at every one of them ourselves.</p>
      <div class="roles">
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The cover that keeps bouncing</h3>
          <p>Wrong colour space, no bleed, a spine built for the wrong page count. Each rejection is another week, and the rejection notice never quite tells you why.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The maths no one taught you</h3>
          <p>Spine width from page count and paper stock, and it is a different number on every shop, because every printer uses different paper. Get it wrong by a hair and the whole cover is wrong.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The ISBN traps</h3>
          <p>Tick one hopeful box for wider reach and Amazon claims your ISBN, and now the shop that actually reaches bookshops and libraries turns you away. Nobody mentioned that on the way in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The silence after launch</h3>
          <p>The book is finally up. And nothing happens. No readers, no plan to find them, and no hours left in the week to learn how. The hardest part turns out to be the part that starts once you are done.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-section how-gates">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>We built the house we wish we had had</h2>
      <p>Murmmers Press is run by authors, for authors. Every wall above, we hit first, with our own books, and it is the reason this house exists. We turned each of those fights into something a machine now does perfectly, every time, so that you never have to.</p>
      <p class="kicker">You should be writing the next one. Not fighting a colour profile at midnight.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we carry, so you do not have to</h2>
      <p class="pl-intro">You hand us a finished manuscript. We carry it the whole rest of the way.</p>
      <div class="roles">
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The edit</h3>
          <p>A close, gentle edit that tightens and polishes and never rewrites. Every change arrives as a visible, justified suggestion you keep or refuse. Nothing is changed behind your back.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The cover and the files</h3>
          <p>A cover made for your book, and every technical version of it the shops demand: the print wrap, the spine to the exact page count, the ebook, all correct the first time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The ISBNs and the shops</h3>
          <p>Your own ISBNs, assigned and managed properly, and your book placed on Amazon, on IngramSpark for the bookshops and libraries, and in our own direct store, without the traps.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="role">
          <h3>The launch, and the long tail</h3>
          <p>A real launch, and a shelf kept lit long after launch week, rather than a book quietly left to sink the day after it goes up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-pull">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="big">And through all of it, one promise above the rest: it still sounds like you.</p>
      <p>The whole house is built around a single rule that outranks every machine in it. Your voice is kept exactly yours. Before a word is read, you set down the spirit of the book and what it must never lose, and that document overrules every agent in the building. No edit may cross it. That is the point of the entire place: to carry a human voice all the way to a reader without ever wearing it smooth.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How it goes</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="s-n">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>You send us the book, and what it means to you</h3>
            <p>A finished manuscript, and a short, honest note on the spirit of it. That note becomes the law of the project.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-n">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>We prepare it, in the open</h3>
            <p>Edit, cover, files, ISBNs, shop listings. Every step visible, every change a suggestion, nothing hidden.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-n">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>You say yes at every gate</h3>
            <p>Nothing moves forward on a machine's say-so. The manuscript, the cover, the price, the launch: each waits for your word.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-n">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Your book goes out, and keeps selling</h3>
            <p>Live on every shop, launched properly, and kept alive. You keep your voice, your rights, your say, and a fair share of every copy sold.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-writers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>We are opening the doors</h2>
      <p>For its first years the list was one author's. It is opening now, to a first few voices, on the same terms we hold ourselves to: your hand on every gate, your voice kept whole, and more of what a reader pays reaching the person who wrote the words. We take on a small number of books at a time, and we begin every one with a conversation, not a contract.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:1.6rem">
        <EmailSignup
          heading="Tell us about your book"
          note="Leave your email and a line about what you have written. We read every one, and we write back."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-name">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="muted">Murmmers Press. Sometimes searched as Murmurs Press. Never mistaken for anyone else.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  .steps li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1.2rem; align-items: start; }
  .steps .s-n {
    width: 2.6rem; height: 2.6rem; flex: 0 0 auto; border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid; place-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--accent-deep, #2b6a5b); color: var(--paper, #fff);
  }
  .steps h3 { margin: .25rem 0 .3rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .steps p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
